  "translations": [
    {
      "verse_no": 160,
      "translation": "Every opposite and by its opposite, know it."
    },
    {
      "verse_no": 161,
      "translation": "For from opposites come opposites."
    },
    {
      "verse_no": 162,
      "translation": "The history of European philosophy is witness to this, that many philosophers and researchers before Hegel's time, had unequal existences."
    },
    {
      "verse_no": 163,
      "translation": "Just as the dual and the plural, objective and subjective, the whole and the part, are not separate. This thought that appearances..."
    },
    {
      "verse_no": 164,
      "translation": "Are interconnected and influence each other. Jalal al-Din Muhammad, Rumi, centuries before Hegel's time, spoke of the constant movement of beings."
    },
    {
      "verse_no": 165,
      "translation": "To which Hegel bestowed the worthy title (Superior Rumi). The grandeur of his great name adorned the veil of history."
    },
    {
      "verse_no": 166,
      "translation": "Referencing Dr. Muhammad Iqbal Lahori, History of Philosophy in India."
